TRENCHRUNNER is released under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD), the most
permissive license the Open Source Initiative approves: no attribution, no
notice preservation, no conditions at all.

That covers the code written for this project: everything under main/, host/,
tools/, components/audio_hal, components/display, components/imu, and the
files core/starwars.h, core/sound.c, core/sound.h, core/pokey.c, core/pokey.h,
core/tms5220.h, core/avg.h and core/autoplay.h.

Two things carry their own licenses, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:

  * core/e6809.c and core/e6809.h are the 6809 CPU core from vecx, which is
    GPL-3.0. Because a build of this project links that core in, the combined
    firmware and host harness must be distributed under the terms of the
    GPL-3.0 as well. Replace that one file with a permissively licensed core
    and the whole project is 0BSD.
  * core/avg.c, core/starwars.c and core/tms5220.c are ports of MAME source
    code, which is BSD-3-Clause and requires the copyright notice to be kept.
    They say so in their headers.

The Star Wars ROM images are not part of this project and are not licensed
by it. They remain the property of their copyright holders.

